one important way the teachers can  enhance a growth mindset is to really  help students self reflect on their own  learning so in the learn storm  activities we tried to be really  intentional about creating a lot of room  for students to engage in  self-reflection and one of our goals in  doing that was to really kind of help  teachers create that really self  reflective environment and really got  the school year started that way and  hopefully that's something that can be  then carried forward for the rest of the  school year it can be really easy to  learn a bunch of stuff and not realize  that you're learning it in the absence  of self reflection so and self  reflection could really help us  recognize what we're doing can help us  connect it to to why we're doing it I  could really help us internalize more  deeply certain ideas when teachers help  students reflect on their own learning  they can think about well what are what  are the goals they have for their  learning and then when as they're going  through and accomplishing their those  goals if students are self reflecting on  that and they're seeing those goals as a  part of being on a growth trajectory  that'll help them get to whether it's a  good grade or becoming a better writer  or or a better mathematician that's  ultimately more motivating for students  and it really helps them see really see  that they're making progress on that  trajectory which is a lot more  motivating they're just kind of taking  off things that don't really seem to be  that related to each other I think one  particularly important kind of  self-reflection is when when students  hear teachers or hear themselves or hear  their peers self reflect on the ways  that struggles help them improve it can  be a really good a good and a really  good reminder that struggles aren't kind  of the endpoint of something that  doesn't struggle doesn't mean that you  should give up and that you're not cut  out to do something but in the contrary  that if we use the right kinds of  strategies and we persist and maybe if  we get help from others and we can  overcome strategies and become better  better learners or better mathematicians  or better at whatever better  skateboarders may be better at whatever  the task might be
 

